# Force LF for every tracked text file, in both the stored blob and the working
# tree, on every OS and regardless of the cloning machine's core.autocrlf. This is
# the same "shape-based, not judgement-based" rule the repo already applies to
# credential handling: one pattern that covers everything, rather than a per-file
# judgement call about which scripts "need" it. .githooks/* is the file that
# actually matters (a CRLF shell script silently stops running, and it's the
# secret guard), but scoping the rule to just that path is exactly the kind of
# narrow pattern that can quietly stop matching what's added next.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never let line-ending handling touch binary assets.
*.png binary
